     "source": "II. Use of English\n                      Maximum score – 20 points / Time – 30 minutes\n\nTask 1. Complete each sentence with the appropriate word from the given variants based\non the context. In the sentences where no word variants are given, add suitable words\nyourself.\n    1. Aliya can speak English ______ (good) than her classmates.\n    2. We ______ (live) in this town since we were children.\n    3. This is the book ______ (add suitable relative clause) was written by my favorite\n        author.\n    4. Everyone was very ______ (interest) in the discussion.\n    5. The problem ______ (solve) before the teacher came.\n    6. He isn’t strong ______ (add suitable adverb) to carry this heavy bag.\n    7. I ______ (do) my homework when my friend called me.\n    8. The tickets ______ (sell) out before we arrived at the cinema.\n    9. She had already ______ (finish) her work when the meeting started.\n    10. Almaty is famous ______ (add correct preposition) its beautiful nature.\n\nTask 2. Read the text below and choose the correct word for each space. For each sentence,\nmark the correct letter A, B, C or D on your answer sheet.\nSpace Exploration\nSpace exploration has always fascinated people because it helps us (11) ______ more about the\nuniverse. Scientists study planets, stars, and galaxies to understand how space (12) ______ and\nhow it began. Many important discoveries have been made thanks to modern technology.\nAstronauts are highly trained professionals who (13) ______ have special preparation before\ngoing into space. Before a mission starts, they must learn how to live and work in zero gravity.\nThey also need to know how to use equipment that (14) ______ designed to work in extreme\nconditions.\n\n\nIn recent years, many space missions (15) ______ launched to explore Mars. Scientists believe\nthat Mars may have had water in the past, which (16) ______ mean that life once existed there.\nBecause of this, robots have been sent to collect samples and send information back to Earth.\nSpace travel is not easy and can be very dangerous. Astronauts often face physical and mental\nchallenges, especially when they (17) ______ been in space for a long time. However, these\nmissions are important because they help improve technology and (18) ______ new knowledge.\nSome people think that space exploration is too expensive, but others believe it is worth the cost.\nIn fact, many technologies we use today (19) ______ developed as a result of space research. I\nbelieve that exploring space is important for (20) ______ future of humanity.\n\n11. A) learn             B) learning              C) learned               D) learns\n12.A) works              B) is working            C) has worked            D) was worked\n13.A) must               B) should                C) can                   D) might\n14.A) is                 B) was                   C) were                  D) has\n15.A) are                B) have been             C) were being            D) had\n16.A) must               B) should                C) could                 D) would\n17.A) have               B) had                   C) will                  D) are\n18.A) create             B) creates               C) created               D) creating\n19.A) are                B) we                    C) have been             D) had been\n20.A) a                  B) an                    C) the                   D) ---",
